window.docContents[106].resolve({"/Elementary-Functions/___4___4-Special-Values-and-Limits/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___4-Special-Values-and-Limits--___4___4_LPAR_ii_RPAR_-Powers":{"contents":"\\[e^0=1.\\]The exponential at zero is one.\n\n\\[e^{\\mathord{\\pm}\\pi i}=-1.\\]Both half-turns on the unit circle map to −1.\n\n\\[e^{\\mathord{\\pm}\\pi i/2}=\\mathord{\\pm}i.\\]The quarter-turn values are the two imaginary units.\n\n\\[e^{2\\pi k i}=1,\\qquad k\\in\\mathbb Z.\\]Every integral number of full turns returns to one.\n\n\\[e^{\\mathord{\\pm}\\pi i/3}=\\tfrac12\\mathbin{\\pm}\\tfrac12\\sqrt3 i.\\]The sixth-turn values have real part 1/2 and imaginary part ±√3/2.\n\n\\[e^{\\mathord{\\pm}2\\pi i/3}=-\\tfrac12\\mathbin{\\pm}\\tfrac12\\sqrt3 i.\\]The third-turn values have real part −1/2 and imaginary part ±√3/2.\n\n\\[e^{\\mathord{\\pm}\\pi i/4}=\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2}\\mathbin{\\pm}\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2}i.\\]The eighth-turn values have equal real and imaginary magnitudes.\n\n\\[e^{\\mathord{\\pm}3\\pi i/4}=-\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2}\\mathbin{\\pm}\\tfrac1{\\sqrt2}i.\\]At three eighths of a turn, the real part is negative and the imaginary part\nhas sign matching the direction of rotation.\n\n\\[i^{\\mathord{\\pm}i}=e^{\\mp\\pi/2}.\\]Using the principal complex power, the two imaginary-unit bases give the\ndisplayed real exponentials.\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions\u0009§4.4 Special Values and Limits","header":"§4.4(ii) Powers","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___4-Special-Values-and-Limits/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___4-Special-Values-and-Limits--___4___4_LPAR_ii_RPAR_-Powers"}});